                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "text_e4EaTU": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>For nearly a decade, MAKE has worked alongside a Level 10 Tea Master in Kyoto. Exceptional tea isn't simply bought, it's entrusted through relationships built over generations. Those relationships have opened doors to teas rarely available outside Japan, allowing us to work with respected producers who share an unwavering commitment to craftsmanship and quality.</p><p>Everything we do is guided by three beliefs:</p><p><strong>We Believe Making Matcha Is as Meaningful as Drinking It</strong></p><p>Preparing a bowl by hand invites you to slow down, if only for a few minutes. Measuring the tea, warming the bowl, whisking until perfectly smooth—each step becomes part of the experience.</p><p>Those few quiet minutes have a way of shaping everything that comes next.</p><p><strong>We Believe Tradition Is a Foundation, Not a Rulebook</strong></p><p>Working alongside our Level 10 Tea Master in Kyoto, we carefully select teas that reflect the highest standards of Japanese craftsmanship. From cultivation and harvest to stone milling and packaging, every decision is guided by flavor, quality, and tradition.</p><p><strong>We Believe Quality Matters More Than Scale</strong></p><p>The finest Japanese matcha has traditionally been prepared at home and in tea houses, where it can be appreciated without compromise. While cafés have introduced millions to matcha worldwide, the realities of speed, consistency, and volume often require a different kind of tea. <br/><br/>We exist to bring the kind traditionally reserved for the bowl into more homes, so more people can experience it as it was intended. This is why you'll rarely find MAKE in cafes.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
